gnome-shell-51.beta's landed a same-day (2026-07-31) 47-commit rewrite of
the GDM greeter's authentication architecture (js/gdm/util.js split into
authServices.js/authServicesLegacy.js/userVerifier.js, plus a new pluggable
mechanism-selection UI via AuthMenuButton). It breaks the default password
login path entirely:

Symptom: GDM shows the user list. Clicking a username (or using "Not
Listed?") starts the PAM conversation correctly -- gdm-password's debug
log shows PAM successfully sending the "Password: " prompt -- but the
GNOME Shell greeter never displays the password entry field, and no
further GNOME Shell/PAM/GDM message appears in the journal at all.
SDDM authenticates the same account/session fine, confirming this is
GNOME Shell greeter-side, not GDM or PAM.

Root cause: in js/gdm/loginDialog.js's _onMechanismsChanged(), the
"selectedMechanism" computed by userVerifier.js (js/gdm/userVerifier.js,
_onMechanismsChanged(): `this.selectedMechanism ?? mechanisms.find(m =>
m.selectable) ?? {}`) is only a *default fallback value for UI display* --
e.g. the lone "Password" mechanism when nothing else is enabled. The
handler only forwards it to the menu button's visual state
(_authMenuButton.setActiveItem()); it never calls
this._selectAuthMechanism(), which is the only path that actually reaches
AuthServices.selectMechanism() and sets the real internal
_selectedMechanism used by the PAM message handlers.

Every PAM prompt handler in js/gdm/authServicesLegacy.js gates on that
real selection, e.g. _handleOnSecretInfoQuery() (which handles
gdm-password's "Password: " prompt):

  _handleOnSecretInfoQuery(serviceName, secretQuestion) {
      if (serviceName !== this._selectedMechanism?.serviceName)
          return;
      ...
  }

With _selectedMechanism never actually set for the auto-selected default
case, this silently drops the prompt -- no signal emitted, no error
logged anywhere, matching the reported symptom exactly. Explicitly
choosing a mechanism via the AuthMenuButton does call
_selectAuthMechanism() (see loginDialog.js's _selectAuthMechanism()), so
that path isn't affected -- only the default/auto-selected case is.

Fix: also call _selectAuthMechanism() with the computed default so the
real internal selection is made, not just the button's visual state.

This is same-day, still-churning upstream code (checked 2026-08-05: no
newer commit touches this code yet), so this is not a backport of an
existing fix -- if upstream lands their own, prefer that instead.

--- a/js/gdm/loginDialog.js	2026-08-06 10:36:45.625653052 +0400
+++ b/js/gdm/loginDialog.js	2026-08-06 10:36:45.639680940 +0400
@@ -1063,8 +1063,21 @@
             }
         }
 
-        if (Object.keys(selectedMechanism).length > 0)
+        if (Object.keys(selectedMechanism).length > 0) {
             this._authMenuButton.setActiveItem(selectedMechanism);
+            // Update the button's visual state above, but selectedMechanism
+            // is only ever a *computed default* here (e.g. the lone
+            // "Password" mechanism when nothing else is enabled) -- it was
+            // never passed through _selectAuthMechanism(), so the backing
+            // AuthServices._selectedMechanism stays null. Every PAM prompt
+            // handler (e.g. _handleOnSecretInfoQuery for the password
+            // prompt) silently drops its message whenever
+            // serviceName !== this._selectedMechanism?.serviceName, so
+            // with no mechanism ever really selected, gdm-password's
+            // "Password: " prompt is dropped with no error anywhere and
+            // the entry field never appears. Actually select it too.
+            this._selectAuthMechanism(selectedMechanism);
+        }
     }
 
     _onDefaultSessionChanged(client, sessionId) {
